{"term":"predict","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c647e7b1abb7c553d0","definition":"To make a prediction: to forecast, foretell, or estimate a future event on the basis of knowledge and reasoning; to prophesy a future event on the basis of mystical knowledge or power.","example":"After he had renounced his fathers bishoprick of Valentia in Spaine... and to attaine by degrees the Maiesty of Cesar, was created Duke of that place, gaue for his poesie, Aut Cesar, aut nihil. which being not fauoured from the heauens, had presently the euent the same predicted.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["foretell","forespell","forespeak","halsen","call","anticipate","augur","bode","divine","forecast","foredeem","forehold","foresee","foreshadow","predict","presage","prognosticate","prophesy"],"antonyms":["retrodict"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["hopedict","mispredict","outpredict","overpredict","predictedly","predicter","predictingly","predictory","repredict","underpredict","underpredicted","underpredicting","unpredict","unpredicted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predict#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a0a474b0088542be43","definition":"To imply.","example":"It is interesting to see how clearly theory predicts the difference between the ascending and descending curves of a dynamo.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["foretell","forespell","forespeak","halsen","call","anticipate","augur","bode","divine","forecast","foredeem","forehold","foresee","foreshadow","predict","presage","prognosticate","prophesy"],"antonyms":["retrodict"],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"transitive, usually","wordFamily":["hopedict","mispredict","outpredict","overpredict","predictedly","predicter","predictingly","predictory","repredict","underpredict","underpredicted","underpredicting","unpredict","unpredicted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","a